    title_en: "EU Product Safety Act (CRA) Mandates Manufacturers to Report Digital Product Vulnerabilities and Severe Incidents Starting in 2026",
    summary_en: "The EU Product Safety Act (CRA) stipulates that starting from September 11, 2026, manufacturers must proactively report any vulnerabilities or severe incidents affecting the safety of their products with digital elements. The reporting mechanism will utilize the CRA Single Reporting Platform (SRP). If 'actively exploited vulnerabilities' are discovered, manufacturers must submit an early warning within 24 hours of becoming aware, followed by a complete notification within 72 hours; the final report must be submitted within 14 days of corrective measures being available. For 'severe incidents,' a final report must be submitted within one month. The reported information will be shared with all relevant regional CSIRTs via the national CSIRT that receives the notification, ensuring timely information dissemination. The European Commission has further regulated the conditions for delaying information dissemination under special circumstances via a delegated act. The implementation of this regulation significantly enhances the cybersecurity transparency and accountability across product supply chains.",
